  "answer": "Both requests have been reported before, but I found no sign that either one has been implemented. (1) Per-keyboard remapping: PowerToys#13378 and #33080 ask for the same thing, and #13378 points to #1460 (Multi Keyboard Support) as the main tracking issue. Keyboard Manager remaps apply to all connected keyboards. Add a thumbs-up to #1460 to help prioritise it. Until it ships, you can't limit a mapping to the Magic Keyboard. (2) Globe/Fn key: in #31832 the Fn key showed as 'Undefined' and wasn't in the key list. The reply there was that, per the docs, the Fn key can't currently be remapped or detected. The reason is that Fn is usually handled in keyboard firmware or drivers and never reaches Windows as a key event. The Globe key on your Magic Keyboard will probably behave the same way. So Globe/Fn+arrow shortcuts aren't possible in Keyboard Manager at the moment. As a workaround, remap other keys you can detect, such as a modifier you don't use, to act as the modifier for Home, End, Page Up and Page Down. Note that this workaround applies to every keyboard."
 },
